From c3395563c24f24e4d2b445af41e4f9a2905baa92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:37:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 021/115] iio: qcom-smgr: add Qualcomm SMGR sensor driver

Adds an IIO driver for the Sensor Manager (SMGR) QMI service exposed
by the Qualcomm Snapdragon Sensor Core (SSC) on msm8998, used on the
Google Pixel 2 XL (taimen) for the accelerometer, gyroscope,
magnetometer, and other SSC-hosted sensors. It talks to the SSC over
QRTR (Qualcomm IPC Router), registering as a qrtr_driver against the
SMGR service/instance and driving it through the qmi_sns_smgr QMI
encode/decode layer added alongside it.

The net/qrtr/smd.c bus rework this driver depends on
(qrtr_driver_register(), struct qrtr_device) now lands in the
preceding "net: qrtr: turn QRTR into a bus" commit, so
__qrtr_driver_register()/qrtr_driver_unregister() resolve.
MODULE_IMPORT_NS(QRTR) is also updated to that commit's string-literal
namespace syntax (MODULE_IMPORT_NS("QRTR")), which is what 6.18
actually expects -- the bare-token form is pre-6.13/v6.0-era and would
not have compiled here regardless of the qrtr bus gap.

Signed-off-by: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
